# Cross-doc consistency

Paths below are relative to the internal docs repo (`deckhouse/storage/internal-docs/state-snapshotter`,
tree `state-snapshotter-rework/`) — see docs-ssot-and-structure. When changing any of:
- `spec/system-spec.md`
- `architecture/overview.md` (or added `system-overview.puml`)
- `design/implementation-plan.md`
- `testing/e2e-testing-strategy.md`
- `operations/project-status.md`

check consistency (no contradiction) at least on:
- registry state vs runtime watch activation
- DSC conditions (`Accepted`, `AccessGranted`, derived `Ready`) and watch activation formula
- optional unified CRD / bootstrap (S1–S2) vs future DSC-driven registry
- manifest / MCR track vs unified snapshot registry (separate concerns)
- stage / progress in `project-status.md` vs tables in `implementation-plan.md` and test IDs in `e2e-testing-strategy.md`

Related long-form ADR (ADR repo, `dkp/storage/state-snapshotter/old2/`) must not disagree with `spec/system-spec.md` without an explicit documented transition.

Fix inconsistencies in the same change or document a temporary divergence and follow-up.
